Cursor-Chrome is an Electron shell that embeds Chromium for local agent control.
It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google LLC, Google
Chrome, the Chromium Authors, or Electron / OpenJS Foundation.

Chromium is included via Electron under Chromium’s BSD-style license. The
required copyright notice, conditions, and disclaimer are in LICENSE.chromium.
The full Chromium third-party credits bundle (`LICENSES.chromium.html`) ships
with Electron binaries and must be retained in binary distributions.
Electron’s MIT license text is in LICENSE.electron.txt.

The agent HTTP API and Chromium remote-debugging port bind to 127.0.0.1 only.
They intentionally have no authentication. Treat them as same-machine power tools:
any local process can drive tabs, read pages, export session cookies, and attach
files from absolute paths the OS user can read. Do not expose ports 9222/9223
to the network.

Third-party components and their licenses are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
and CREDITS.md.
